<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Decision Intelligence Simulation Lab | Portfolio App</title>

<style>
body { margin:0; font-family:Arial; background:#0b1a2a; color:#f5f5f5; }
header { background:#2b1b12; padding:20px; text-align:center; }
.container { display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(340px,1fr)); gap:20px; padding:20px; }
.card { background:#12263a; padding:20px; border-radius:12px; }
input, textarea, select {
  width:100%; padding:10px; margin-top:10px;
  border:none; border-radius:6px;
  background:#2b1b12; color:#fff;
}
button { margin-top:10px; padding:10px; width:100%; background:#3a6ea5; border:none; color:#fff; border-radius:6px; cursor:pointer; }
.metric { font-size:18px; margin-top:10px; }
.small { font-size:13px; opacity:0.85; margin-top:8px; line-height:1.4; }
.resultBlock { margin-top:10px; font-size:14px; line-height:1.5; }
.history { max-height:180px; overflow-y:auto; font-size:13px; }
hr { border:0; border-top:1px solid #2b1b12; margin:10px 0; }
</style>
</head>

<body>

<header>
<h1>Decision Intelligence Simulation Lab</h1>
<p>Model decisions, simulate outcomes, and understand the logic behind consequences</p>
</header>

<div class="container">

<div class="card">
<h3>1. Decision Input Layer</h3>

<div class="small">
This system models decisions as structured variables. Instead of guessing outcomes, you define measurable conditions that influence probability.
</div>

<input id="decision" placeholder="Decision (e.g. Start SaaS business)">

<select id="domain">
<option>Business</option>
<option>Career</option>
<option>Education</option>
<option>Personal Development</option>
<option>Investment</option>
</select>

<input id="risk" type="number" placeholder="Risk Level (1-10)">
<input id="time" type="number" placeholder="Time Investment (hours/week)">
<input id="skill" type="number" placeholder="Skill Level (1-10)">
<textarea id="notes" placeholder="Context, assumptions, constraints"></textarea>

<button onclick="simulate()">Run Simulation</button>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>2. Outcome Engine</h3>

<div class="small">
Outcomes are not predictions—they are weighted simulations based on input variables. Higher skill and time increase success probability, while higher risk introduces volatility.
</div>

<div class="metric" id="success"></div>
<div class="metric" id="failure"></div>
<div class="metric" id="volatility"></div>

<hr>

<div class="resultBlock" id="logicBreakdown"></div>

</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>3. Impact Analysis Layer</h3>

<div class="small">
Impact measures the potential magnitude of success or failure, not just probability. High-impact decisions can change trajectory even at lower success rates.
</div>

<div class="metric" id="impact"></div>
<div class="metric" id="confidence"></div>
<div class="metric" id="readiness"></div>

</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>4. Behavioral Intelligence Insights</h3>

<div class="small">
This layer interprets patterns in your decision style over time. It identifies whether you tend toward risk avoidance, overconfidence, or under-preparation.
</div>

<div class="resultBlock" id="insights"></div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>5. Simulation History</h3>
<div class="history" id="history"></div>
<button onclick="clearHistory()">Clear History</button>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>6. Documentation: Why This System Exists</h3>

<div class="resultBlock">
Most people make decisions emotionally or based on incomplete information. This system replaces intuition-only thinking with structured reasoning.

<hr>

<b>Core Purpose:</b>
- Convert abstract decisions into measurable variables
- Simulate possible outcomes before commitment
- Reduce impulsive decision-making
- Improve long-term strategic thinking

<hr>

<b>Design Philosophy:</b>
This tool does not claim to predict the future. Instead, it models probability distributions based on input constraints.

Each decision is treated as a system:
<ul>
<li>Inputs = risk, time, skill, domain</li>
<li>Process = weighted probability engine</li>
<li>Output = success/failure likelihood + impact score</li>
</ul>

<hr>

<b>Intended Use Case:</b>
- Entrepreneurs evaluating ideas
- Students choosing learning paths
- Professionals assessing career moves
- Individuals testing life decisions before committing

<hr>

<b>Important Limitation:</b>
This system does not account for unpredictable external events (market shifts, human randomness, timing effects). It is a structured thinking aid—not a deterministic predictor.
</div>

</div>

</div>

<script>
let historyData = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('decisions_v2')||'[]');

function simulate(){
 let decision = document.getElementById('decision').value;
 let domain = document.getElementById('domain').value;
 let risk = Number(document.getElementById('risk').value);
 let time = Number(document.getElementById('time').value);
 let skill = Number(document.getElementById('skill').value);
 let notes = document.getElementById('notes').value;

 if(!decision || !risk || !time || !skill) return alert('Complete all fields');

 let base = 50;
 let success = Math.max(0, Math.min(100,
   base + (skill*4) + (time*1.5) - (risk*5)
 ));

 let failure = 100 - success;
 let volatility = Math.min(100, risk*10 + (10-skill)*5);

 let impact = Math.round((time * risk * skill)/3);
 let confidence = Math.round((skill*10 + (100-risk))/2);
 let readiness = Math.round((skill*6 + time*2)/2);

 document.getElementById('success').innerText = "Success Probability: " + success + "%";
 document.getElementById('failure').innerText = "Failure Probability: " + failure + "%";
 document.getElementById('volatility').innerText = "Volatility Index: " + volatility;
 document.getElementById('impact').innerText = "Impact Score: " + impact;
 document.getElementById('confidence').innerText = "Confidence Level: " + confidence + "%";
 document.getElementById('readiness').innerText = "Readiness Score: " + readiness + "%";

 document.getElementById('logicBreakdown').innerHTML =
 "Success increases with skill and time investment, and decreases with risk exposure. Volatility measures unpredictability introduced by high risk and low skill alignment.";

 let insight = "";
 if(skill < 4) insight += "Low skill baseline increases uncertainty.<br>";
 if(risk > 7) insight += "High risk behavior detected—results may vary significantly.<br>";
 if(time < 5) insight += "Low time investment reduces outcome stability.<br>";
 if(success > 70) insight += "Decision structure is strong and well-balanced.<br>";

 document.getElementById('insights').innerHTML = insight;

 historyData.push({decision, domain, risk, time, skill, success, impact, date:new Date().toISOString()});
 localStorage.setItem('decisions_v2', JSON.stringify(historyData));
 renderHistory();
}

function renderHistory(){
 let div = document.getElementById('history');
 div.innerHTML = '';
 historyData.slice().reverse().forEach(d=>{
  let el = document.createElement('div');
  el.innerText = `${d.date.split('T')[0]} | ${d.decision} | S:${d.success}% | I:${d.impact}`;
  div.appendChild(el);
 });
}

function clearHistory(){
 localStorage.removeItem('decisions_v2');
 historyData = [];
 renderHistory();
}

renderHistory();
</script>

</body>
</html>
